AB  - The recognition and classification of facial expressions using artificial intelligence (AI) presents a promising avenue for early detection and monitoring  of neurodegenerative disorders. This narrative review critically examines the  current state of AI-driven facial expression analysis in the context of  neurodegenerative diseases, such as Alzheimer's and Parkinson's. We discuss  the potential of AI techniques, including deep learning and computer vision, to  accurately interpret and categorize subtle changes in facial expressions  associated with these pathological conditions. Furthermore, we explore  the role of facial expression recognition as a noninvasive, cost-effective tool  for screening, disease progression tracking, and personalized intervention in  neurodegenerative disorders. The review also addresses the challenges, ethical  considerations, and future prospects of integrating AI-based facial expression  analysis into clinical practice for early intervention and improved quality of  life for individuals at risk of or affected by neurodegenerative diseases.
DO  - 10.1515/revneuro-2024-0125
