AB  - BACKGROUND: Early detection of depression is very important for the treatment of patients. In view of the current inefficient screening methods for depression,  the research of depression identification technology is a complex problem with  application value. METHODS: Our research propose a new experimental method for  depression detection based on audio and text. 160 Chinese subjects are  investigated in this study. It is worth noting that we propose a text reading  experiment to make subjects emotions change rapidly. It will be called Segmental  Emotional Speech Experiment (SESE) below. We extract 384-dimensional Low-level  audio features to find the differences of different emotional change in SESE. At  the same time, our research propose a multi-modal fusion method based on  DeepSpectrum features and word vector features to detect depression by using deep  learning. RESULTS: Our experiment proved that SESE can improve the recognition  accuracy of depression and found differences in Low-level audio features. Case  group and Control group, gender and age are grouped for verification. It is also  satisfactory that the multi-modal fusion model achieves accuracy of 0.912 and F1  score of 0.906. CONCLUSIONS: Our contribution is twofold. First, we propose and  verify SESE, which can provide a new experimental idea for the follow-up  researchers. Secondly, a new efficient multi-modal depression recognition model  is proposed.
DO  - 10.1016/j.jad.2021.08.090
