AB  - When patients with cancer develop depression, it is often left untreated. We developed a prediction model for depression risk within the first month after  starting cancer treatment using machine learning and Natural Language Processing  (NLP) models. The LASSO logistic regression model based on structured data  performed well, whereas the NLP model based on only clinician notes did poorly.  After further validation, prediction models for depression risk could lead to  earlier identification and treatment of vulnerable patients, ultimately improving  cancer care and treatment adherence.
DO  - 10.3233/SHTI230274
