AB  - Artificial Intelligence systems often exhibit a deficient comprehension of human emotions, leading to restricted contextual engagement and empathic response capacities. The incorporation of Emotional Intelligence into AI systems is crucial for allowing robots to comprehend, adjust to, and react to human emotions with appropriateness and sensitivity. Hume AI methodologies provide a data-centric framework for modelling emotional granularity via facial expressions, voice intonations, and language indicators, enabling emotionally attuned responses. The materials and techniques include the implementation of multimodal emotion detection systems using Hume’s emotion API, which analyses real-time audiovisual data via deep learning models trained on varied affective datasets. Feature extraction, sentiment weighting, and emotion categorization are integrated with reward mechanisms to provide adaptive behavioral responses in AI agents. Implementation tactics emphasize real-time processing, cultural flexibility, and ethical concerns, establishing the foundation for emotionally intelligent AI that may improve social interaction in areas such as mental health, customer service, and education.
