AB  - Learning is not only about being able to access information, but health and adaptive support. Technology and conventional learning methods do not all the time fulfill the requirements of individuals or respond to the emotional condition of the learners, thus can affect motivation and learning outcomes. This paper is discussing a smart study aide, Study Mate, which aids in aiding learning as well as health. Study Mate helps student plan their study programs and have tailor-made schedules, adaptive quizzes, and summarized study notes. It also informs and educates on some of the problems, and it makes the process of learning more interactive and understandable. In addition to the academic guidance, Study Mate tracks the activity levels of students and the increased levels of stress to offer suggestions of staying focused and motivated. Through the learning support and monitoring of the state of emotions, the platform encourages better self-regulation and studying practices. Study Mate will be simplified and made user friendly; therefore, it is available to learners with different learning styles. This application is expected to be more productive, understanding and self-confidence to enable students feel supported throughout their learning process. In the paper, the nature and history and some of the background impact of Study Mate is described, in how a thoughtful, student-focused product has the potential to develop a more personalized, effective, and emotionally balanced learning.
