AB  - This project introduces Emotibuddie, a multimodal and multilingual AI system that detects emotions and stress levels while offering personalized support for mental wellness. Unlike typical systems that use only one type of input, Emotibuddie can accept text, voice, or facial image input for a more flexible emotional assessment. It employs pre-trained models, such as BERT, wav2vec, and CNNs, to analyse inputs. A Generative AI model, creates motivational responses and CBT-based micro-tasks. These are then translated into various Indian regional languages using the Google Translate API to maintain cultural relevance. The system design features an API-based modular structure, prompt engineering, and multilingual delivery. This creates a scalable base for future real-time use in mental health applications.
