AB  - DeepPainSense is an intelligentsystem that operates in real time to identify chronic pain as well as emotional conditions like stress and anxiety through a multimodal strategy. It gets information from three main sources: facial expressions from a camera, body movements from motion sensors, and muscle activity from sensors that measure muscle movement. muscle activity (monitored through EMG sensors). Advanced deep learning methods are employed to analyze these signals, utilizing ResNet-50 combined with LSTM for facial recognition, BiLSTM or Transformer models for recognizing motion patterns, and ID CNN with LSTM for processing muscle signals. For precise predictions, an attention-based fusion layer integrates all feature outputs. The system can tell when there is pain and also notice actions like guarding, limping, or bracing, and it checks how bad the pain is. It also uses multitask learning to identify emotional states, which helpes in fully understanding both the patient's physical and mental health. DeepPainSense also incorporates Explainable AI (XAI) through tools like SHAP and LIME, which clarify the rationale behind each prediction, fostering trust among both users and healthcare professionals. Real-time feedback is given via a chatbot or voice assistant, which is especially helpful for home physiotherapy, remote monitoring, and taking care of elderly people.
