AB  - This paper presents an emotion-aware AI agent designed to provide empathetic mental health support with cultural, situational, and contextual awareness. The proposed system integrates multimodal emotion recognition by combining text, speech, and facial expression analysis with a culturally adaptive natural language processing framework. By leveraging real-time user inputs and ambient contextual cues, the agent dynamically adapts its therapeutic dialogue and guidance strategies. Key features include a journaling module for identifying emotional patterns and a dual-interaction mechanism that enables user feedback through text or audio. The agent delivers brief, personalized interventions such as cognitive behavioral exercises and mindfulness-based techniques tailored to individual needs. By promoting emotional self-awareness, resilience, and sustained mental well-being, the proposed approach aims to support inclusive and context-sensitive mental health assistance.
