AB  - Mental healthcare chatbots are artificially intelligent systems that have been built with the intent of simulating human conversation and provide emotional support to one’s user. They are also widely used as tools to help individuals cope with the stress, anxiety, and other mental health challenges they have been facing, including easily accessible and affordable solutions. These chatbots use NLP and emotion recognition technology to assist users in understanding their feelings and responding accordingly. This review unpacks the latest advancements of recently developed chatbots, such as GPT-4-based models, BERT and MBERT based models, sentiment analysis, and the study of multimodal systems combining text, voice, and facial expression recognition. Also addressed are important challenges, including privacy concerns, cultural inclusivity, and clinical validation. Finally, the review identifies opportunities to improve chatbots, including supporting multi-language and primary telehealth platforms and customizing user interaction with chatbots to create more inclusive and effective mental health support worldwide.
