AB  - In today’s world, mental health has become a pressing global issue, affecting people across all age groups and walks of life. 15% of India’s adult population experiences mental health issues. According to Indian journal of Psychiatry India has 0.75 psychiatrists per 100,000 people whereas WHO recommends at least 3 per 100,000. Despite of increasing awareness, access to effective mental health care remains limited due to factors such as high costs, lack of availability and persistent social stigma. The social stigma generally leads people to push themselves to not express their thoughts and feelings and prevent individuals from seeking timely support, leading to prolonged emotional distress and reduced quality of life. In today’s fast-paced and digitally connected world, there is a need for solutions that are not effective but also accessible, affordable and stigma-free. Advancements in Artificial Intelligence, especially in the fields of Natural Language Processing (NLP) have opened up new possibilities for mental health support. This paper proposes the development and application of a sentiment-aware chatbot- an AI-powered virtual assistant designed to understand to users’ emotional support, especially during moments when professional help is not immediately available. Ultimately, this technology aims to bridge the gap between traditional mental health services and the daily emotional needs of individuals fostering a culture where mental well-being is prioritized, supported and destigmatized.
