AB  - Multimodal emotion analysis, a key area of affective computing, integrates textual, audio, and visual information to support applications like human-computer interaction and mental health monitoring. Challenges such as modality redundancy and dynamic emotional changes in conversations limit the efficiency and robustness of existing methods, requiring improved fusion strategies and models. This paper proposes a novel multimodal sentiments recognition model by using Graph Neural Networks (GNNs) to enhance intra-modal contextual dependencies and a Multi-head Attention Mechanism (Multi-Attn) to deep cross-modal interactions. Additionally, we introduces two innovative loss Soft-HGR and SWFC to optimize sentiments recognition performance. Our experiments on the IEMOCAP and MELD datasets show that the proposed model outperforms existing baselines, robustness, and adaptability. This paper presents a novel approach for multimodal sentiment analysis, combining Graph Neural Networks (GNNs) and Multi-head Attention (MultiAttn) to enhance feature modeling and reduce modality redundancy. Innovative loss functions (Soft-HGR and SWFC) further improve consistency, achieving superior performance on benchmark datasets.
