AB  - Addressing mental health challenges like depression and addiction requires timely, empathetic, and privacy-preserving support. Traditional digital systems often fail to recognize emotions in real time, reducing their impact. This paper presents NextZen AI, a multimodal framework for real-time emotion monitoring in mental health applications. It integrates wav2vec2 (voice), FaceAPI (facial expressions), and LLaMA 3.1 (text sentiment) through a Weighted Multimodal Emotion Fusion (WMEF) mechanism to generate context-aware responses. Experiments using RAVDESS, FER-2013, and GoEmotions datasets show high accuracy (94 % facial, 91 % speech) and low latency. Real-world deployment achieved 78% reconnection success, 82 % positive sentiment, and NPS 72, validating NextZen AI as an effective, scalable, and privacycompliant emotion-aware mental health support system.
