AB  - Artificial Intelligence (AI) has evolved at a very fast pace, and one of the prominent innovations in the human-computer interaction is emotion-sensitive chatbots, which will help people communicate more naturally and sympathetically. This paper seeks to explore the application of emotion recognition through Natural Language Processing (NLP)-based techniques in improving the interaction between humans and AI by allowing chatbots to identify, read, and react to the emotions of users. It uses multimodal approach, which incorporates text-based sentiment analysis, voice features and optional facial expression to develop and test an emotion conscious chatbot. To determine the performance of chatbots in regards to the accuracy of emotion detection, user satisfaction, relevance of response, and engagement, a sample of 300 users in the spheres of healthcare, education, and customer service was involved. The results indicate that multimodal emotion detection is always more effective than unimodal ones, which results in the increased accuracy in emotion detection (up to 88 percent), higher user satisfaction (average 4.3/5), increased relevance of responses, and increased engagement. The study concludes that emotion-aware NLP chatbots can transform human-AI communication by providing personalized, empathetic, and context-aware responses, emphasizing the need for ethical design and responsible data management.
