AB  - As the integration of digital tools within organization continues to grow at an alarming rate, there has been a dramatic rise in the deterioration of mental health. People place a greater emphasis on their professional obligations rather than their physical well-being; thus, creating more psychological problems and lessening the amount of mental peace within Society. While AI tools provide ways for improving productivity, many fail to account for the detrimental effects on people’s mental health. This system will have three main components: the User Input Module, the AI Analysis Engine, and the Intervention Module. The User Input Module will allow for gathering multimodal data (text, voice, and images) using various means. The AI Analysis Engine will analyze the data collected from these inputs in order to recognize the different levels of emotion present and identify common negative recurring conditions such as frequent anger. Finally, the Intervention Module will provide users with an automated alert and provide tailored recommendations for each user so that they may learn how to self-regulate themselves. The paper will provide insight into how this project can help create a healthier and happier society through providing people with simple and easy-to-access tools for relaxation purposes.
