AB  - In recent times, there has been a rapid growth of mental health issues among individuals worldwide. A growing proportion of the population is facing difficulties with emotional instability, depression, psychological strain and many more. These can be solved only by providing a supportive response to the user. In the early days, there was only processing of text-based requests, but as time changed, multiple modalities, such as audio and video, were also being accepted as user requests. The responses are also generated according to the input taken from the user. This paper surveys the advancements in text, audio and video emotions recognition which focusing on deep learning models, attention mechanisms and multimodal fusion techniques. Pre-trained models are used to demonstrate superior performance across multiple benchmark datasets. Despite the advancements, challenges remain in real-time deployment, like data imbalance, cross-model alignment and scenarios. Research Challenges, Future enhancements are illustrated to enhance and propose optimal model in the area of multimodal Natural Language Processing(NLP).
