AB  - Mental health and emotional well-being are fundamental to daily functioning. For years, musical expression and experiences have been regarded as a beneficial method of emotional regulation. When listening to music, if we are able to anticipate a listener’s emotional state and contextualize that state within the music recommendation system, this will improve the music offers/viewing solutions presented to the listener. The goal of the "Emuse" project is to automatically provide an emotional assessment and use that assessment to make music recommendations. eMUSE is platform, that can make recommendation decisions based on raw data, extracting real-time emotional assessments from facial expressions. Through the application of Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN), we detect emotions and classify their expression through bi-modal facial features (e.g., mouth, eyes). The emotions originally identified included, but were not limited to, happiness, sadness, anger, surprise, and neutrality concurrent to music genres. An original CNN model was trained using facial datasets with high accuracy classification of the emotional states. The eMUSE system demonstrated it was able to detect emotions, and in return to make an emotional music selection offer. The eMUSE system is unique, as it can combine for simultaneous audio analysis and emotion for subsequent music selection making to enhance the user’s experience in real time. Moreover, eMUSE may be appropriate as an element within mobile applications or streaming services that could offer listeners emotionally relevant playlists for any given mood. It may also be possible that emotion recognition could be devised in a multi-modal manner, incorporating facial affect and voice or written text to enhance recommendations based on the optimal emotional detection, and provide further recommendation adaptations.
