AB  - Mental health is crucial for overall well-being, impacting individuals and society significantly. Prioritizing mental well-being and early addressing of underlying issues is essential, as prolonged neglect can greatly affect overall health. This research paper explores the implantation of a multimodal approach comprising facial expressions, tone of voice, and texts using a DNN (Deep Neural Network) model to predict emotions. The predicting emotions encompass six basic categories: happiness, sadness, anger, disgust, fear, and neutrality. It also employs reinforcement learning to predict personalized activities based on the emotional state. Furthermore, the study presents novel contributions in gender-based comparison exploring the role of gender in emotional expression and enhancing the efficiency and accuracy of emotion prediction. These advancements contribute to the state-of-the-art in emotion recognition and personalized activity recommendation. The results indicate that the multimodal approach, which incorporates gender as a factor, exhibited higher accuracy in predicting emotions compared to the general modal that did not consider gender.
