AB  - This paper introduces an integrated therapeutic chatbot system that combines facial emotion recognition, personality analysis, and conversational AI to offer personalized mental health care. The system employs a VGG16 architecture modified to emotion detection with enhanced accuracy (92.8% compared to baseline 87.5%), and MBTI personality analysis from linguistic patterns. The chatbot supports both online (OpenAI API) and offline (pre-trained NLP model) modes, and offers continuous therapeutic conversation based on identified emotions and chat history. Additional features include health monitoring through pulse and posture analysis, access to resources, and journaling. Experimental results show substantial improvements in emotion recognition accuracy and user engagement compared to current systems. The proposed solution offers a comprehensive, accessible, and privacy-aware solution to mental health care, especially beneficial in areas with limited access to professional psychological services.
