AB  - Mental health conditions, such as anxiety, depression, and stress, often remain untreated due to stigma, fear, or limited access to professional care. This research proposes an Artificial Intelligence based framework to provide scalable, empathetic, and explainable mental health support. The model integrates Natural Language Processing (NLP) for sentiment and emotion analysis, Explainable AI (XAI) for transparent predictions, and behavioral monitoring to assess user habits. The framework adopts a multi-phase approach, starting with a baseline Naive Bayes model for sentiment classification and evolving into advanced transformer-based architectures for emotion recognition. Anomaly detection algorithms are employed to analyze behavioral patterns, offering personalized recommendations. Evaluation results demonstrate the model's efficacy and potential to strengthened traditional mental health care systems. We aim to achieve a sentiment analysis accuracy of 91% and 65% improvement in user trust through ExplainableAI techniques, to offer superior sentiment analysis and unique behavioral monitoring in comparison to existing models like Woebot and Wysa.
