AB  - Emotion recognition plays a crucial role in various fields, such as intelligent human-computer interaction, mental health monitoring, and intelligent customer service. Traditional emotion recognition methods mainly rely on unimodal input, including facial expressions or voice signals, which may limit recognition accuracy. In contrast, multimodal emotion recognition, by integrating voice, facial expressions, and physiological signals, significantly enhances both accuracy and robustness. This paper reviews the fundamental theories, key technologies, and practical applications of multimodal emotion recognition, with a focus on the integration of voice, facial expression, and physiological signal recognition technologies. It also explores future trends and challenges in the field.
