AB  - Often, especially in rural areas, students do not receive the support they need for mental health issues. Stigma, a lack of knowledge, and restricted access to specialists all contribute to this problem. A mixed AI-driven system for proactive emotional support and mental health monitoring is presented in this paper. It uses a mix of spoken, facial, and textual emotional cues. The system consists of two parts: (i) a text analysis component based on Natural Language Processing (NLP) that uses facial expression recognition to identify emotional states like sadness, anxiety, and distress in real time and (ii) a MATLAB facial emotion recognition module that can identify signs of negative emotions or suicidal risk by analyzing social media posts. The identified emotions are processed by a recommendation engine, which then offers culturally appropriate audio, video, or textbased interventions to enhance wellbeing. The system instantly notifies parents or teachers in emergency situations so they can take prompt action. Furthermore, a mood history tracking feature ensures that students’ mental health is continuously monitored by enabling stakeholders to examine emotional trends over time. This project integrates textual and facial cues to create a coherent framework. This approach enables the AI chatbot to understand its environment and respond culturally sensitively. Additionally, it can offer easily accessible, reasonably priced, and personalized mental health support to students in rural areas.
