AB  - Recently, the number of the online videos is booming. However, its openness gives the horror clips a chance to threaten children's physical and mental health. Therefore, it is necessary to design an algorithm to filter the horror clips in online videos. In this paper, we proposed a multimodal multilevel attention neural network for horror clip detection. Information from visual modality and auditory modality is used to describe the various factor of horror, including violence, bloody, deformed human, scream, sudden sound, etc. The temporal-level attention is designed to give the model the ability to capture horror moments. The modal-level attention automatically balances the weight on all modalities. We evaluate the model on the same dataset used in MediaEval 2017 Emotional Impact of Movies Task. The experimental result shows the advantages of our proposed model compared with other groups.
