AB  - Emotion recognition has emerged as a significant challenge in the field of human-machine interaction. Recent advancements in artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML) have enabled more accurate analysis and identification of emotions, particularly in women. This review article explores AI and ML-based methods and techniques for emotion recognition in women. A comprehensive literature review is conducted, examining various approaches, including natural language processing (NLP), facial analysis, and voice analysis. Specific challenges related to emotion recognition in women, such as cultural and gender differences, are analyzed. Furthermore, potential applications of these technologies in areas such as mental health, marketing, and recommendation systems are discussed. The findings suggest that combining multimodal data and employing deep learning models can significantly enhance the accuracy of emotion recognition. However, further research is needed to improve models, develop specialized datasets, and address ethical and privacy concerns. This article serves as a reference for researchers and developers interested in advancing this field. This article reviews the latest papers published in 2023 in databases such as Google Scholar, PubMed, IEEE Xplore, and Springer.
DO  - 10.1109/IPRIA68579.2025.11263538
