AB  - Background: Stress impacts our mental and emotional equilibrium daily. Accurate assessment methods are crucial for effective stress management.Purposes: This research integrates a structured questionnaire with real-time camera tracking to evaluate stress levels. It aims to Evaluate the combined effectiveness of self-reported data and facial expression analysis and Assess the accuracy of various machine learning methods in classifying stress levels.Methods: The system uses a questionnaire and real-time video monitoring to record facial expressions. Machine learning methods, including Random Forest, k-Nearest Neighbors (KNN), Support Vector Machines (SVM), and Naive Bayes, analyze stress ratings. The facial expression analysis achieves a 63.2 percent accuracy rate in detecting stress.Results: Combining questionnaire data with facial expression analysis provides a detailed stress assessment. The integration of these methods allows for a comprehensive evaluation, highlighting the potential for personalized stress management strategies.Conclusions: This method offers a comprehensive evaluation of stress, enhancing precision and enabling tailored stress management techniques. Further improvements could increase accuracy and effectiveness.
