AB  - This research presents a multimodal AI-driven supportive system designed to assist neurologists in diagnosing anxiety disorders in neurologically affected patients. The proposed system integrates audio features, facial action units, and textual transcripts from clinical interviews to detect and classify three primary anxiety disorders: generalized anxiety disorder, social anxiety, and panic disorder. The methodology combines unsupervised clustering to identify distinct anxiety disorders with supervised ensemble classification for accurate prediction of different anxiety disorders. Feature-level analysis and explainable AI techniques provide insights into the key factors influencing each disorders supporting neurologists in clinical decision-making. Evaluated on the DAIC-WOZ dataset, the system demonstrates high accuracy and robustness, enabling early identification of this important comorbidity for proper referral and monitor progress.
