AB  - This study addresses issues such as insufficient accuracy in emotional monitoring for the elderly by designing an intelligent monitoring system based on multimodal data fusion and convolutional neural networks (CNN). The system integrates multi-source data including heart rate, blood pressure, and facial expressions to construct a multi-branch convolutional neural network model. This model comprises physiological feature branches and facial expression feature branches, which extract features from different modalities respectively. Subsequently, feature fusion and classification modules perform information integration and emotion classification decisions. During the experimental phase, model training was conducted using the TensorFlow 2.x framework and Keras API, employing the Adam optimizer and sparse category cross-entropy loss function. Model performance was evaluated using a 5-fold cross-validation strategy. The model achieved an average accuracy of $87.33 \%$ and an F1 score of $86.17 \%$, fully validating the feasibility and effectiveness of multimodal data fusion and convolutional neural networks in elderly emotion recognition tasks.
