AB  - Human feelings have a profound influence on mental health, productivity, and general behavior in day-to-day life. Music can be found to regulate mood and offer psychological comfort. Existing music suggestion algorithms, though, are only based upon user liking or usage history, and neglect the user’s current emotional state, which incapacitates them to be capable of offering true psychological care. Our research outlines a multimodal emotion recognition for music recommendation and affective state estimation system with facial expression recognition and vocal tone analysis and a music recommendation system. Facial expressions are recorded through a webcam and voice responses through a microphone every few minutes, analyzed with deep learning models to estimate affective states, and contextually appropriate music is recommended for instant affect change. The mechanism of detection at the rear is strong, using a Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) for Speech Emotion Recognition (SER) and Facial Emotion Recognition (FER), and a deep learning-based model (CNN) for Speech Emotion Recognition (SER) based on acoustic features extracted from MFCC, Pitch, and Chroma. On top of this, it creates an emotional summary for each day and personal recommendations for every user by means of a Mental Health Dashboard from which users may see mood patterns and improve well-being. The integration of computer vision, speech processing, and intelligent recommendation algorithms enables the paper to suggest a real- time adaptive personalized emotionaware assistant for application in mental well-being support and lifestyle enrichment.
