AB  - Stress, anxiety, and depression increasingly impact individual well-being and organizational performance, but traditional methods like counselling and questionnaires tend to be reactive and subjective. The Emotion and Cognitive Stress Radar (ECSR) is a multimodal system to measure emotional and cognitive states in real time unobtrusively using facial, speech, text, physiological, and behavioral signals. Assessed on both institutional and benchmark datasets, ECSR proves to be more accurate and reliable than single-source systems. Its adaptive dashboards accommodate personalized insights, early intervention, and organizational well-being tracking, fostering proactive and scalable mental health monitoring model.
