AB  - In recent years, with the accelerated pace of social life and the increase in sources of pressure, psychological stress has become a common social issue, seriously affecting people's physical and mental health. Traditional methods of psychological stress intervention have their limitations, which has led to widespread attention on the application of Virtual Reality (VR) technology instress relief. VR technology, by creating an immersive virtual environment and integrating physiological signals (such as EEG, ECG, skin conductance, etc.) and behavioral signals (such as facial expressions, voice, eye movements, etc.), enables precise identification and real-time intervention of an individual’s emotional state, making it an effective means of alleviating psychological stress. This article reviews the research progress of VR-based psychological stress relief, with a focus on emotion models, the application of multimodal signals in emotion recognition, and the associated challenges. It also looks ahead to future research directions. By analyzing existing multi modal emotion recognition methods and their application in VR, the article points out the issues of signal inconsistency and data redundancy in current methods and proposes improvements. Future research needs to focus on the fusion of multimodal signals at different levels of strategy, combined with deep learning for dimensionality reduction, to effectively address issues such as differing representation dimensions and redundant data. This will enhance the application effectiveness and social value of VR in the field of mental health. © 2025, John Wiley and Sons Inc. All rights reserved.
