AB  - I) A recent area that is very closely related to sentiment analysis is Text-Based Emotion Detection and Recognition from Text (known as emotion analysis). Emotion analysis is related to recognising emotions in text and to differentiate between these emotions i.e. surprise, anger, disgust, fear, joy, sadness, or neutral, while sentiment analysis aims to find positive, neutral or negative attitude in text. Multimodal Emotion Identification is related to classify input video sequences into emotion labels using video, audio and/or text input. FER has many applications including diagnosis of mental disorders and may also be helpful to facilitate the study of social and physiological interactions between humans. By using speech recognition, staff can sense how the customers are feeling and take the necessary actions with the purpose to enhance a customer experience and infections convert the visitors to clients, while text recognition can be used in online education, data mining, human-computer interaction (HCI), information filtering systems and psychology. With the presented implementation of the discussed emotional recognition system, a case study of building a multimodal system is presented, which is capable of detecting emotions from any input format. Multimodal HCI technologies can make the human-computer interaction much more natural. Human-computer interaction (HCI) aims to unite people and computers, where one of the tools might be human interfaces (like how we interact with smartphones, clinometer, airplane cockpit and so on). Another area related to this research is how to create new forms and the best way to make interaction with technology (called interaction technology). One type of interaction with humans and technology is related to "exposure to input", where computer detects what types of input from a human and use this data to accomplish the needs of a user. Another goal of the HCI is to present machine's output in most practical and understandable way. By real time capturing facial expressions and voice input, emotions can be detected, and system can reflect the results in real time as well, when the emotions are changing or new input detected. Detailed description of the experiments depicts over than 85% of the accuracy by deep learning model.  © 2025 Author(s).
