AB  - Depression as a disorder has always been a focus of attention of researchers. Depressive disorders and mental health issues are the major problems. These disorders affect large community such as children’s, middle aged group, teenagers, low-income group, farmers. Depression is also associated with noncommunicable diseases, chronic communicable diseases, physical disorders. Poverty and poor health due to unbalanced Economic conditions is also one of the causes of depression. Several pharmacological interventions are available for managing depressive disorders. Various artificial intelligent systems are available to predict depression level of a person such as by analyzing his/her facial expressions, vocal expressions, speech analysis, sentiment analysis, ECG data, EEG data, heart rate, blood pressure. But people suffering from depressive disorders are unable to avail good quality health care due to many unavoidable reasons, it creates treatment gap. 87.2–95.7% treatment gap for depression was reported in India from community-based studies [“Depression in India-Let’s talk” World Health Organization, India]. This fact leads to focus more on preventive measures. In India, depression level in females of 40–49 age groups is much more than males according to survey of NMHS 2015–16 findings [“Depression in India-Let’s talk” World Health Organization, India]. More research is needed in this era to prevent depressive disorders and provide healing hand with smart care facilities. Main challenge is to transform scientific and engineering knowledge into action to form effective Detection system. This paper focuses on statistical survey of India. Types of depression and various depression causing factors and various modes are highlighted with which depression can be detected. © 2022, The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG.
