AB  - Most of people engaged in public speaking to large or small groups who often experienced severe physical symptoms of anxiety such as blushing, shaking, pounding heart, and quivering voice et al. Some organizations such as Toastmaster international try to help people to improve their public speaking skills by providing a supportive and positive environment for individual to practice, and speakers could receive feedback from their peers on their performance during each meeting. It is expected that there is a tool which could provide assessment more often, easy and without anybody help. Assessing speaking ability is complex, involving both feature extraction from unimodal data such as text, speech, and images, and fusion of cross-modal data, and is a challenging problem to be solved in the field of multimodal learning analytics. In this paper, we first design different feature extraction models for the three modalities of visual, auditory and textual information. The proposed facial feature extraction model based on improved PFLD is able to use a multi-scale region learning strategy to better capture the details and differences of facial features and enhance the extraction of visual features. The proposed Transformer-TCN speech feature extraction model consists of an encoder module, a feature fusion module, and a time-domain convolutional network, which improves the accuracy and reliability when processing time-series data. Thirdly, we used a pre-trained BERT model with a 12-layer Transformer structure for text feature extraction. Based on the extracted features from three modalities, this paper proposes a TMJP(Tri-Modal Joint Representation) learning method based on the cross-modal Transformer, which is centered on the cross-modal attention mechanism. The cross-modal attention mechanism adapts the flow from one modality to another by focusing on information from different modalities. Comparative experiments demonstrate that the proposed TMJP public speech evaluation model achieves the best performance in all three metrics compared to other multimodal analysis models, and could be used for Toastmasters students public speaking evaluation tool. When more modal data are available in the future, it is flexible to extend to four, five modal data or even more based on the design principle of the method. © 2025 IEEE.
