AB  - With the rapid advancements in Artificial Intelligence (AI) technology and Internet of Medical Things (IoMT), multi modal emotion recognition is emerging as a key tool for enhancing the quality of patient care in the healthcare sector. By integrating facial expressions, speech, physiological signals (e.g., heart rate, electroencephalogram), and text analytics, multimodal emotion recognition (MER) provides a more comprehensive and accurate understanding of patients' emotional states to support diagnosis and personalized treatment. Although unimodal emotion recognition techniques have made progress in some applications, however, the integration and application of multimodal approaches in healthcare remains a relatively novel research area. This study systematically examined the current state of MER technology in healthcare, focusing on the potential value of this technology in the areas of mental health monitoring, chronic disease management, elder care, employee emotion management and patient satisfaction. The paper also explores the latest technological advances in (MER) systems combined with IoMT, including the use of deep learning models, data collection fromIo MT, and cross-modal data fusion techniques. Despite the promising outlook of the field, it also faces challenges such as data privacy, clinical integration, and model interpretability. This review aims to provide a comprehensive overview of the current technological landscape and discusses the future directions of (MER) in healthcare, emphasizing its transformative potential for patient care. © 2025, John Wiley and Sons Inc. All rights reserved.
