AB  - Lack of communication increases health risks such as depression and dementia, making conversational partners essential for elderly support. Conversational agents or robots have the potential to assist in this area. To achieve natural human-agent listening interactions, appropriate responses to the human speaker’s level of engagement are essential. This study investigates the effectiveness of integrating recently emerging LLM-based features into engagement estimation. Three machine learning experiments are conducted to compare various architectural designs using non-verbal video and audio features (facial expressions, gaze, head movements, and prosody), partial or full utterances, and time-series or flattened fixed-size vectors. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2026.
